    "body": "I've updated to follow the XDG-spec. It should respect the `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME` and fallback to `$HOME/.config` if the env is not set. I actually don't like to use the platform-native via `dirs` because on `macOS` we still use `~/.config` for TUI application.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if it could break current user config in case they have `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME` in different place but `starship.toml` still in `~/.config`. Should I keep the default for it?",
    "created_at": "2023-07-06T13:15:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-06T13:25:13Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/5282#discussion_r1254423212",
